{"id": "8b8529ee-5e35-4023-803b-bb592f4ea5dc", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check this for you. I'll look at Bedrock usage in us-east-1 over the last 14 days. That means the invocation metrics, the model invocation logging setup and any CloudTrail data events. Then I'll sort the calls by whether they used a direct model ID or an inference profile.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_S6cK6D0w9P8axbKyBfoi77", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-model-id-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["searching-logs", "exploring-metrics", "investigating-infrastructure-changes", "verifying-with-docs"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Audit Amazon Bedrock runtime usage in us-east-1 to find calls that use a direct foundation model ID (e.g. anthropic.claude-...) where an inference profile (cross-region/system-defined 'us.'/'global.' prefixed profile or application inference profile) should be used instead. Report which callers/principals/applications, which model IDs, and call volumes.",
  "context": "User asks: 'Are any of our Bedrock calls in us-east-1 using a direct model ID where we should be using an inference profile? Check the last 14 days.' This is a scoped audit, not a root-cause hunt. Agent space account is 123456789012 (region us-east-1); also check any other associated AWS accounts via list_associations if they exist. Note: Bedrock InvokeModel/Converse are data events in CloudTrail (only visible if data event logging is enabled on a trail/event data store), so also check whether Bedrock model invocation logging is enabled (bedrock get_model_invocation_logging_configuration) and, if it delivers to CloudWatch Logs, query the log group with Logs Insights for modelId, identity.arn, operation over the window. Also use CloudWatch AWS/Bedrock metrics (Invocations by ModelId dimension): inference profile usage shows ModelId as the profile id/ARN, direct usage shows the bare foundation model ID. If S3 is the logging destination, sample recent objects if feasible. Also use bedrock list_inference_profiles and list_foundation_models (inferenceTypesSupported) to determine which models used directly are ones that REQUIRE an inference profile (inferenceTypesSupported lacks ON_DEMAND) vs. those where direct on-demand is allowed but a profile is merely optional/recommended. Be clear about which source gave each conclusion and any visibility gaps (e.g. logging not enabled).",
  "resources": ["AWS_ACCOUNT:123456789012", "bedrock", "us-east-1"],
  "timeframe": "2026-11-09T21:19:35Z/2026-11-23T21:19:35Z",
  "criteria": "List each direct model ID seen, call counts, calling principals/roles if available, whether that model requires an inference profile or supports on-demand, and the matching inference profile that should be used. Note any errors (ValidationException about on-demand throughput) if visible. Read-only only."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit Bedrock us-east-1 calls for direct model ID usage"}], "created_at": null}

